        "problem": "Find the first four non-zero terms of the Maclaurin expansion of $\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{3}}.$",
        "worked_solution": "The standard Maclaurin expansion for $\\frac{1}{1-x}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & =1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nReplacing $x$ with ${x}^{3}$ in the above expansion and simplifying gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{3}} & =1+({x}^{3})+{({x}^{3})}^{2}+{({x}^{3})}^{3}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1+{x}^{3}+{x}^{6}+{x}^{9}+\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
